Well, my promising caveman died after getting mobbed in a treasure room
(or just outside it).  He only had an AC of -1, but he had the +5
Grayswandir and an amulet of reflection so I thought he could handle
it.  He was surrounded and had wounded legs.  I spent the last turn
removing a cursed scroll of teleportation from my blessed BoH so I
could escape.  But it never occured to me to *pray* or even better,
*burn Elbereth* with my wand of fire, which I kept in my main inventory
for just that purpose.  I guess I didn't think the situation was that
dangerous, but then his hp dropped like a rock.  If I'd taken a second
to really think about what was going on I could've lived and probably
ascended this character.  He had reflection, +5 Grayswandir, a blessed
BoH, and a magic lamp for a MR wish.  I didn't know it, but I had =oSD,
which I wanted since I was getting hungry a lot.

And he had a ton of scrolls.  This is because I spent a *long time*
stealing every scroll from a huge bookstore on D2.  Then I ID'ed them
all with a B?oID.  I also credit cloned and bought out a general store
on D3, a tool store on D4, and another general store on D6.  And I
converted the altar on D3 and got Grayswandir right away.  It would've
taken me through the rest of the game no problem!

*Sigh*

